# Normalise every text file to LF in the working tree.
#
# This repository commits a built artifact (lib/) that must be byte-identical
# to what a rebuild produces on any machine, and CI asserts exactly that with
# `git diff --exit-code -- lib/`. Two things broke that on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true:
#
#  1. git reported lib/client.js as modified on a clean checkout — same size,
#     same content, differing only in the EOL it would apply next checkout.
#  2. lib/client.js.map embeds the sources verbatim in `sourcesContent`, so a
#     CRLF working tree produced a map that Linux (LF) could never reproduce.
#
# Forcing LF everywhere makes the checkout — and therefore the artifact —
# platform-independent. Source files are stored as LF in the index already, so
# this changes the working tree, not history.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Media is binary; keep git from inspecting or converting it.
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary
